1. **Independence Date:** India gained independence on **August 15, 1947** (not 1946). 
2. **First President:** India did not become a republic until **January 26, 1950**, when its Constitution came into effect. 

Therefore, the **first President of India** was **Dr. Rajendra Prasad**, who took office on January 26, 1950. 

Between August 15, 1947, and January 26, 1950, India was a Dominion within the British Commonwealth, and the head of state was the British Monarch (King George VI), who was represented in India by a Governor-General (Lord Mountbatten and then C. Rajagopalachari). The head of government during this time was Prime Minister Jawaharlal Nehru.


